hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20626","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, from an uncle called Jariyah ibn Qudamah al-Sa'di, that he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, say to me a word that will benefit me and keep it brief for me, perhaps I will retain it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not get angry. He repeated it to him many times, each time he said: Do not get angry."
"20627","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Hisham informed us, my father informed me, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, from an uncle of his called Jariyah ibn Qudamah, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, say to me a word and keep it brief for me, and he mentioned the hadith."
"20628","He said: Yahya narrated to us, thus Hisham said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, and they say he did not meet the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), meaning Yahya ibn Sa'id says: and they say."
"20629","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, from Jariyah ibn Qudamah, he said: And an uncle of mine narrated to me that he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me something that will benefit me and keep it brief, and he mentioned the hadith."
